  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "Earth Day is celebrated annually on April 22 to demonstrate support for environmental protection, with over 1 billion people participating globally. Founded in 1970 by Senator Gaylord Nelson, it serves to raise awareness about pollution, climate change, and conservation through activities like tree planting, cleanups, and educational campaigns managed by EarthDay.org. Key Aspects of Earth Day Purpose: The day aims to catalyze action for a healthy, sustainable environment, often focusing on issues like plastic pollution, climate education, and reforestation.Origin: The first Earth Day was held on April 22, 1970, in the United States, following a massive oil spill in Santa Barbara, California. It mobilized 20 million people and led to the creation of the EPA. Global Impact: More than 192 countries participate in events, including street marches, conferences, and environmental workshops.How to Contribute: Individuals can make a difference by planting trees, recycling, switching to sustainable energy, reducing plastic use, and participating in local cleanups. Earth Day 2026 Focus and ActionFor 2026, campaigns focus on ambitious goals such as cleaning up millions of pounds of waste and investing in global reforestation through projects like The Canopy Project. Organizations worldwide, such as the Earth Day Initiative, host virtual and in-person events, including festivals and educational panels.",
